description=Ties trade and crafting skills to the traits and profession picked at character creation. Pips in a skill set both a one-time starting level and a max level cap (0 pips=4, 1=5, 2=7, 3=9, 4+=10). Taking even 1 point in a linked skill (e.g. Cooking/Butchering, Blacksmithing/Welding) raises the paired skill's cap by 1. Four optional training traits (Experienced, Self Taught, Unfinished Education, Blank Slate) tune how much of that starting level you actually begin with, without ever changing the cap. A server-wide toggle can remove those four training traits from character creation entirely, and the no-trait baseline starting levels are now their own sandbox options instead of only being hardcoded. Character creation now previews every trade skill as a 10-square bar (green = starting level, yellow = still trainable, red = capped), and the in-game skills panel marks capped squares red too. Combat, running, sneaking, and other physical/agility skills are unaffected. Only trade/crafting skills (plus Maintenance) are capped. Built for Project Zomboid Build 42 multiplayer, where every character otherwise ends up maxing every craft skill regardless of backstory. Created for Terror AustraliZ RP: https://terroraustraliz.com. Released under the MIT license. Report issues at https://github.com/phoenixdoll/Jack-Of-Some-Trades.
